  "lead_analysis": [
    "Under the fragmentation-neutral RPE the 10k ranking is COLMAP (10s RMSE 0.305 m, coverage 0.931) < C' (0.374 m, 0.752) < native E2E (0.428 m, 0.931) < D (1.261 m, 0.815) < B6 (3.923 m) < A (6.236 m). C' remains better than D, so the C' decision stands, but C' covers 18 points less of the 10 s pairs than COLMAP and has larger 10 s error: no COLMAP parity claim.",
    "D's 1 s RMSE (0.412 m) exceeds its 1 s p95 (0.341 m): errors are dominated by a small number of gross outlier pairs (rank-0 component 1 s RMSE 0.449 m vs p95 0.249 m; the 814-image component with Sim(3) scale 0.649 has 1 s p95 2.12 m). The D base graph fixes metric scale but the mapper still produces local pose jumps/drift; that is the next GT-free diagnosis target.",
    "5k D beats the 5k gap46 configuration on both windows (10 s RMSE 0.426 vs 3.525 m at similar coverage 0.826 vs 0.815).",
    "corridor1-5: C' is not better than A/B6 on RPE either (10 s RMSE 1.104 vs 1.039 m), consistent with the failed holdout gates."
